A database is the backbone of persistent, reliable data storage — handling volumes and consistency guarantees that go far beyond what in-memory storage can offer.

Client → Server → Database (Read/Write) → Server → Client

𝗘𝘅𝗮𝗺𝗽𝗹𝗲:
Every "Add to Cart" click on an e-commerce platform is a database write. Every product page load is a database read.

𝗪𝗵𝘆 𝗶𝘁 𝗺𝗮𝘁𝘁𝗲𝗿𝘀:
Choosing the right database type — SQL, NoSQL, or beyond — is one of the highest-leverage decisions in system design, directly shaping scalability, consistency, and long-term maintainability.

